# Keep Docs Specs Updated

- When implementation changes affect product behavior, data flow, or architecture, review the related `docs/*.md` spec files in the same task.
- This is especially important for changes to the analysis or topic modelling pipeline, workspace flow, report generation, prompts, schemas, and exported outputs.
- If a relevant spec already exists, update it so it matches the shipped behavior and naming.
- If a major workflow or subsystem changes and no matching spec exists yet, add a new Markdown spec in `docs/` instead of leaving the behavior undocumented.
- Do not leave stale specs behind after code changes.
